From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone-1.2: modem ring indicator wakes the phone

The EG25-G's RI line reaches PL6 on the 1.2 board: a 120 ms low pulse for
an SMS and one every 6 s while a call rings (tested with gpiomon; the
modem's "risignaltype" is "physical", "urc/ri/smsincoming" a 120 ms pulse).
Mainline describes none of the modem's lines. As a gpio-keys key with
wakeup-source, both wake the phone from sleep. PL6 is in the always-on
domain (R_PIO), as the 1.2 board moved RI there for deep sleep.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone-1.2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone-1.2.dts
@@ -43,6 +43,23 @@
 		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
 		reset-gpios = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PL2 */
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The modem's ring indicator, RI: a 120 ms low pulse for an SMS, and one every
+	 * 6 s while a call rings (the EG25-G's "risignaltype" is "physical"). A wakeup
+	 * source, so that both wake the phone from sleep. PL6 is in the always-on domain
+	 * (R_PIO), for deep sleep.
+	 */
+	modem-ri {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		key-ri {
+			label = "Modem RI";
+			gpios = <&r_pio 0 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PL6 */
+			linux,code = <KEY_WAKEUP>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
